  "fab_notes": [
    "1. Material: FR-4, 1.6 mm, 4 layers, JLCPCB JLC04161H-7628 stackup (sheet 2 table).",
    "2. Copper: 1 oz outer, 0.5 oz inner. Surface finish: lead-free HASL.",
    "3. Solder mask green, silkscreen white, both sides. Vias tented.",
    "4. Fabricate to IPC-6012 Class 2. Electrical test 100 %.",
    "5. Dimensions in mm. Tolerances unless noted: outline ±0.2, finished holes ±0.08.",
    "6. Fabricate from the Gerber and drill files of the same revision as this drawing.",
    "7. Minimum trace width 0.20 mm. Smallest hole Ø0.30 (vias) on Ø0.61 pads: 0.15 mm annular ring.",
    "8. No mounting holes, slots, controlled impedance, castellations, edge plating or gold fingers."
  ],
  "bom_notes": [
    "1. INSTALLED BY: JLCPCB = fitted by the JLCPCB assemblers (SMT and through-hole) before delivery; After delivery = fitted by the builder.",
    "2. PROCESS gives the assembly process and the side the part is on.",
    "3. The motorized fader VR1 is fitted after delivery (KC-01-1870 item 2), and the handle at module level.",
    "4. U5, U7, U8, U10 and U11 are the panel switch terminal blocks.",
    "5. Substitutes need the approval of the design authority."
  ],
  "assembler": "JLCPCB",
  "after_delivery": [
    "VR1"
  ],
  "place_polarised": [
    "D1",
    "C14"
  ],
  "place_label_size": 1.2,
  "place_notes": [
    "1. VR1 (fader) is on the top side; every other part is on the bottom side. Each side is shown in two overlapping parts, top half and bottom half.",
    "2. The bottom view is drawn as seen holding the board bottom side up (flipped left to right), so the datum is at the top right.",
    "3. Red dot = pin 1 of every part with more than two pins, the cathode (pin 1) of D1 and the + terminal (pin 1) of C14. These match the silkscreen marks.",
    "4. LED1 (red) and LED2 (green) are anti-parallel across the motor; fit them to the silkscreen polarity marks.",
    "5. Terminals U5, U7, U8, U10, U11: 1 and 3 +5V, 2 switch input, 4 lamp return (switched by Q1–Q5).",
    "6. Part centres, rotations and part numbers are in the placement table (last sheets), measured from the datum (top view)."
  ],
